# Finance Operator Experience Structure v1

## Framing

The Experience Model defined *how* operators think (sequence, verdict, owner, lane).

This document defines *what information must be available, in what cognitive order and grouping*, for that thinking to be possible — still without screens, navigation, or implementation.

**Structure question:**

> What information constellation must a Financial Case expose so the North Star is answerable without entity archaeology?

---

# 1. Information Architecture Principles

## IP1 — Case-shaped information, not entity-shaped information

Information is organized around **one registration’s Financial Case**. Payment, receipt, schedule, and ledger facts are **attributes/evidence of the case**, not peer “homes” of understanding.

## IP2 — First-class vs contextual vs altitude-bound

| Class | Definition | Rule |
| ----- | ---------- | ---- |
| **First-class** | Required to form verdict + next-action owner for daily cases | Must be present in case comprehension before action |
| **Contextual** | Improves priority, amount judgment, or handoff clarity | Present when relevant; must not bury first-class truths |
| **Altitude-bound** | Meaningful only in exception or audit lanes | Must not dominate daily case reading |

## IP3 — Reading order is part of the structure

Structure encodes the Experience Model sequence. Reordering so that settlement badge or ledger precedes eligibility/policy is a structural failure, not a preference.

## IP4 — Composition slots, not merged fields

Each first-class layer maps to a **composition slot** that keeps its domain SoT. Structure composes slots into a narrative; it does not invent a unified status field.

## IP5 — Owner and lane are information, not footnotes

Next-action owner and work lane are first-class outputs of case structure (derived), equal in importance to settlement and proof.

## First-class information (must)

| Slot | Content |
| ---- | ------- |
| Identity | Member + tour + departure context |
| Eligibility | Booking lifecycle (read-only for finance meaning) |
| Collection policy | Offline due vs no money due (free/zero) |
| Money target | Obligation + remaining (and whether personalized) |
| Proof progress | none / in review / rejected / accepted |
| Open intent (as ingress detail) | Whether a Payment intent is open + whether it is manual-exception vs default path |
| Settlement meaning | Club badge unsettled / partial / settled — with coexistence note when needed |
| Partial scope | When partial: which layer |
| Next-action owner | member / finance / lifecycle_desk / policy_system / exception_policy / idle |
| Work lane | daily / exception / audit |
| Case verdict seed | Composed “where we are” classification (mental, not new SoT enum) |

## Contextual information (supporting)

| Slot | When needed |
| ---- | ----------- |
| Party size | Obligation explanation |
| Obligation source | Tour price vs override |
| Proof artifact / member note | During finance-owned review |
| Payment amount vs obligation | Amount judgment on review |
| Installment plan presence | Only if schedule-active for this case |
| Urgency (departure proximity) | Prioritization among cases — not settlement definition |
| Manual-intent provenance | When V-INTENT-OPEN or duplicate risk |

## Exception / audit-only information

| Slot | Lane |
| ---- | ---- |
| Terminal + leftover money-object meaning | Exception |
| Duplicate / parallel Payment intents | Exception |
| Persistent unexplained layer conflict | Exception → Audit |
| Ledger journal lines / outbox events | Audit |
| Reconciliation findings | Audit |
| Deep idempotency / technical sync forensics | Audit / debugging (outside operator daily structure) |

---

# 2. Financial Case Information Hierarchy

Cognitive priority order (locked):

```text
Identity
→ Eligibility & Collection Policy
→ Money Target
→ Proof Progress
→ Settlement Meaning
→ Next Action Owner
→ Exception / Audit Context
```

Open intent and partial scope attach under Proof Progress / Settlement Meaning as subordinate slots (see below). Work lane is derived alongside Next Action Owner.

---

### L1 — Identity

| Dimension | Content |
| --------- | ------- |
| **Why needed** | Anchors the case; enables club handoff without UUID-as-story |
| **If missing** | Operator works an orphan proof/payment; wrong-person risk |
| **Must never override** | Must not replace money truths; identity alone never answers North Star |

---

### L2 — Eligibility & Collection Policy

| Dimension | Content |
| --------- | ------- |
| **Why needed** | Frames whether money path is allowed and whether money is due at all |
| **If missing** | Blame member for unpaid while still pending approval; chase free/zero cases; treat closed cases as daily collection |
| **Must never override** | Must not be overridden by unpaid badge or open Payment intent (“they owe” while not eligible / no money due) |

**Sub-slots:** lifecycle eligibility (`not_yet` / `eligible` / `closed`) · policy (`offline_due` / `no_money_due`).

---

### L3 — Money Target

| Dimension | Content |
| --------- | ------- |
| **Why needed** | Defines owed amount and remainder for proof judgment and partial meaning |
| **If missing** | Approve/reject without amount anchor; confuse tour list price with personal obligation |
| **Must never override** | Must not be overridden by settlement badge (“paid” does not redefine what was owed); badge ≠ target |

**Sub-slots:** obligation · remaining · personalization flag/source.

---

### L4 — Proof Progress

| Dimension | Content |
| --------- | ------- |
| **Why needed** | Core ingress signal for offline Denali; decides finance vs member ownership |
| **If missing** | Empty queue misread as finance backlog; cannot distinguish awaiting member vs awaiting finance |
| **Must never override** | Must not override eligibility/policy (proof on terminal case does not restore daily happy path); must not alone mean “payment OK” |

**Sub-slots:** proof state · open intent detail · (contextual) proof amount vs obligation.

---

### L5 — Settlement Meaning

| Dimension | Content |
| --------- | ------- |
| **Why needed** | Club badge answer for “is the registration treated as settled?” |
| **If missing** | Cannot answer leaders reliably; post-decision trust wobble |
| **Must never override** | Must not override proof-in-review ownership (unpaid during review is normal); must not override money target |

**Sub-slots:** unsettled / partial / settled · healthy coexistence flag when unpaid + in_review · partial scope when partial.

---

### L6 — Next Action Owner

| Dimension | Content |
| --------- | ------- |
| **Why needed** | Second half of North Star; converts understanding into effort allocation |
| **If missing** | Finance does member work or waits while proof sits; manual payment invented to “own” the case |
| **Must never override** | Owner derivation must not be overridden by which entity the operator happened to look at first |

Derived per Experience Model priority (terminal → proof in review → eligibility → policy → rejected → member/idle/partial).

---

### L7 — Exception / Audit Context

| Dimension | Content |
| --------- | ------- |
| **Why needed** | Marks when daily composition is insufficient; prevents false confidence |
| **If missing** | Terminal leftovers processed as normal reviews; mismatches chased as member delinquency |
| **Must never override** | Must not invade daily cases as default noise; presence of ledger capability must not pull L7 above L2–L6 in daily reading |

Only after L1–L6 fail to produce a coherent daily verdict/owner — or when terminal/conflict cues fire.

---

## Hierarchy diagram

```text
[L1 Identity]
     ↓
[L2 Eligibility + Policy] ──── gates money blame
     ↓
[L3 Money Target]
     ↓
[L4 Proof Progress (+ open intent)]
     ↓
[L5 Settlement Meaning (+ partial scope)]
     ↓
[L6 Next Action Owner + Work Lane]
     ↓
[L7 Exception/Audit Context] ── only when needed
```

---

# 3. Case Story Composition Model

## Purpose

Turn separate SoTs into **one operator narrative sentence** without collapsing enums.

## Anti-pattern vs required narrative

| Bad (entity/status fragment) | Good (composed case story) |
| ---------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| “Payment pending” | “Registration approved, money due, receipt not submitted — waiting for member” |
| “Unpaid” | “Club settlement unsettled; proof with finance for review — normal, finance owns next action” |
| “Approved” | “Registration approved” **or** “Transfer proof approved” — never bare |
| “Pending” | “Waiting for club acceptance” / “Waiting for member proof” / “Waiting for finance review” |
| “Partial” | “Case partially settled; remainder X” **or** “Installment 2 partial” |
| “Paid” on free tour | “Settled — no payment required” |
| “Receipt pending” on cancelled | “Registration cancelled; leftover proof needs exception judgment — not daily review” |

## Composition rules

### R1 — Healthy coexistence

When proof is in review and club settlement is unsettled:

> Narrate **both**, mark **non-alarming**, owner = **finance**.

Forbidden: narrating this as sync failure or member failure.

### R2 — Object-qualified language

Every wait/approval/paid/partial token in the story must name its object (Operator Language Rules). Structure must reserve distinct slots so language can stay qualified.

### R3 — Partial scope

If settlement or recognition is incomplete, story must include scope before owner claims:

- case settlement partial, and/or
- obligation remainder, and/or
- installment slice, and/or
- wallet progress

Unscoped “partial” is an incomplete case story.

### R4 — Free / zero cases

Story pattern:

> “Registration eligible; **no money due**; club settlement settled — idle on money.”

Forbidden patterns: awaiting member proof; awaiting finance review; “paid because transfer captured” when no capture occurred.

### R5 — Terminal cases

Story pattern:

> “Registration **closed** (cancelled/rejected).”  
> If money objects remain: append “**exception**: leftover money object requires policy judgment.”

Forbidden: same narrative template as daily V-AWAITING-FINANCE.

### R6 — Manual intent without proof

Story pattern:

> “Registration approved, money due, **open payment intent**, receipt not in review — waiting for member (intent alone is not settlement).”

Forbidden: treating open intent as finance review due.

### R7 — North Star completeness

A composed story is incomplete unless it states:

1. where we are (verdict-class meaning), and  
2. whose next action it is.

### R8 — Evidence vs headline

Entity names may appear as evidence footnotes in the operator’s mind; they must not be the **headline** of the case story.

---

# 4. Daily Work Information Boundary

## Belongs to daily operator understanding

| Information cluster | Supports |
| ------------------- | -------- |
| Full L1–L6 case hierarchy | North Star |
| Proof review package (artifact + obligation + eligibility) | J1 |
| Awaiting-member meaning (no proof / rejected proof) | J2, J3 |
| Settlement answer + coexistence note | J4 |
| Next-action owner + lane = daily | Effort allocation |
| Free/zero as no-chase settled | P08 |
| Scoped partial when relevant | J7 |
| Awareness that manual payment is exception/alternate | J5 |

## Does not belong to daily understanding (as primary content)

| Information cluster | Why excluded from daily primary |
| ------------------- | --------------------------------- |
| Ledger line archaeology | Audit altitude |
| Reconciliation investigation as morning default | Exception/audit |
| Historical cleanup of terminal leftovers as unmarked queue meaning | Exception |
| Technical sync forensics / idempotency keys as operator story | Debugging |
| Browsing finance entities detached from a case | Violates case unit |
| Treating schedule generation/waive as default daily ingress for Denali offline happy path | Secondary unless schedule-active and scoped |

## Daily structural test

If removing ledger/recon/historical-cleanup information still leaves L1–L6 + composed story + owner intact, daily structure is healthy.

---

# 5. Exception Information Boundary

A case **leaves normal daily interpretation** when any of the following information cues appear. Structure must surface the cue as **lane = exception** before happy-path verbs (approve/reject as routine).

| Cue | Why daily interpretation stops |
| --- | ------------------------------ |
| **Terminal lifecycle + money objects** (e.g. historical pending receipt) | Commercial meaning of capture is ambiguous; P14 |
| **Duplicate / parallel intents** (manual + member path ambiguity) | Unclear which ingress is authoritative |
| **Conflicting truths unexplained by healthy coexistence rules** | e.g. not the normal unpaid+in_review pattern |
| **Unexplained mismatch** after an action that should have settled the case | Trust/coherence failure → exception then possibly audit |
| **Policy dispute** (should this have been free/zero / override?) | Not a proof-quality decision alone |

## Exception information that becomes first-class (only in this lane)

- Explicit “commercial meaning unclear” flag in the case story  
- Inventory of conflicting slots (which layers disagree)  
- Provenance of intents/proofs relative to lifecycle timestamps  
- Required decision type: policy judgment vs cleanup vs escalate to audit  

## Exception does not mean

- Delete domain objects  
- Merge statuses to hide conflict  
- Silently continue daily approve habits  

---

# 6. Audit Information Boundary

## When audit concepts become relevant

| Trigger | Audit information role |
| ------- | ---------------------- |
| Daily composition cannot explain settlement vs capture | Verify journal / projection coherence |
| Reconciliation finding exists for the case/tour | Exception triage at accounting altitude |
| Post-capture trust still broken after case story shows settled | Confirm outbox/ledger without making it the club answer |
| Suspected double-entry / duplicate credit issues | Accounting investigation |

## Why audit must not dominate daily decisions

1. **North Star altitude:** Club questions are answered from settlement + proof + owner, not journal lines.  
2. **Cognitive cost:** Ledger detail buries L2–L6 and recreates entity-browser behavior.  
3. **False dependency:** Operators learn to “need ledger” to believe normal outcomes (Problem H / P12 failure).  
4. **Non-goal:** Structure must not become an accounting dashboard.

## Audit placement rule

Audit information is **opt-in altitude** after exception cues or explicit mismatch — never a peer first-class slot in the default case hierarchy.

---

# 7. Information Omission Risks

| Missing layer | Operator misunderstanding | Wrong action | Business risk |
| ------------- | ------------------------- | ------------ | ------------- |
| **Identity** | Treats queue object as abstract task | Reviews wrong person’s money | Mis-capture / privacy / trust loss |
| **Eligibility** | Reads unpaid as member failure | Chases or opens payment too early | Member harassment; process noise |
| **Collection policy** | Assumes every settled needs a receipt | Waits in proof queue for free/zero | Wasted ops time; false incident reports |
| **Money target** | Guesses amount from memory/tour list | Approves wrong amount / misses underpay | Revenue leakage or unfair reject |
| **Proof progress** | Infers activity only from unpaid badge | Creates manual payment or “sync bug” chase | Duplicate intents; distrust |
| **Settlement meaning** | Cannot answer “payment OK?” | Inconsistent club go/no-go | Departure / leadership errors |
| **Coexistence note** (when unpaid+in_review) | Assumes system broken | Re-checks endlessly / double work | Throughput collapse |
| **Partial scope** | Thinks “partially paid” is enough/not enough wrongly | Clears or blocks departure incorrectly | Safety/ops/finance misalignment |
| **Next-action owner** | Assumes whoever is on-screen owns work | Finance does member job or ignores proof queue | Backlog + member frustration |
| **Exception cues** | Treats terminal leftover as daily proof | Approves commercially dubious capture | Accounting/policy incidents |
| **Audit boundary (wrongly omitting when needed)** | Accepts incoherent layers | Closes case while mismatch remains | Silent integrity failure |
| **Audit boundary (wrongly including always)** | Believes daily needs journal | Avoids finance tools or over-investigates | Slow ops; altitude collapse |

---

# 8. Acceptance Criteria

Any future experience structure (still pre-visual) is acceptable **only if**:

1. **Case as unit** — Information is organized so a registration case is the comprehension unit; entity facts appear as case evidence.  
2. **North Star completeness** — Structure always affords both “where we are” and “whose next action.”  
3. **Hierarchy fidelity** — Default reading order matches L1→L7; settlement/ledger cannot outrank eligibility/policy.  
4. **First-class completeness** — All first-class slots (§1) can be populated for active daily cases.  
5. **Ownership clarity** — Next-action owner is an explicit structural output, not inferred only from which list the operator opened.  
6. **Status separation** — Composition slots remain distinct; no unified finance status replaces lifecycle/payment/receipt/settlement SoTs.  
7. **Healthy coexistence expressible** — Unpaid + proof in review can be represented as normal finance-owned work.  
8. **Object-qualified narrative support** — Structure supplies objects needed for Language Rules (what is pending/approved/paid/partial).  
9. **Partial scope slot** — Incomplete settlement cannot be told without scope.  
10. **Free/zero non-chase** — No-money-due cases structurally differ from awaiting-member.  
11. **Daily/exception/audit separation** — Boundaries in §§4–6 are enforceable in the information model (lane is knowable).  
12. **Terminal exception marking** — Terminal + money objects cannot share unmarked daily proof-review meaning.  
13. **Bookings/Finance boundaries** — Lifecycle remains eligibility input; finance does not gain lifecycle-transition meaning; bookings do not gain receipt-capture meaning.  
14. **Audit non-dominance** — Daily case comprehension remains intact without ledger/recon primary content.  
15. **Post-decision coherence slot** — After finance accepts proof, settlement meaning is part of the same case story operators used to act.  
16. **Manual intent demotion** — Open manual payment without proof does not structurally equal “finance must review now.”

---

# 9. Explicit Non-goals

This Experience Structure **must not become**:

| Non-goal | Why |
| -------- | --- |
| **A replacement domain model** | Domain SoTs stay authoritative; structure only composes them for humans |
| **A unified finance status system** | Would merge axes and violate Non-Goals / P03 |
| **An accounting dashboard** | Ledger/recon are audit altitude, not daily case structure |
| **An entity browser** | Browsing payments/receipts/ledger rows as primary IA reintroduces translation burden |
| **A Bookings takeover surface** | Lifecycle ownership unchanged |
| **A screen, sitemap, or navigation proposal** | Still discovery; Interaction Concepts come only after acceptance |
| **A schema/API redesign brief** | No implementation artifacts in this phase |
| **A mandate to delete installments/prepayments from domain** | They remain contextual/secondary unless schedule-active |

---

## Structure one-liner

> A Financial Case exposes a fixed hierarchy of composition slots — identity, eligibility/policy, money target, proof progress, settlement meaning, next-action owner, then exception/audit context — so operators can narrate one object-qualified story without merging truths or climbing to ledger altitude for daily work.

